    "reply": {
      "changeSets": {
        "1": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The new rules are in Tier 2. Oldest-first allocation of payments to fines and the Unpaid/PartlyPaid/FullyPaid classification are in `Accounts.fineCover` (src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs, diff lines 108-125). The 'settled by this payment' set is derived in `Payments.pay` (diff lines 148-154). Tier 3 `Views.account` only maps the cover union to display strings (`| Accounts.FullyPaid -> \"paid\"`). `Views.ofPayment` only maps the settled fines to copy ids. The CLI only joins the strings. No Tier 3/4 site re-derives a rule.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "No new effect is introduced. `fineCover` and the settled computation are pure functions of the `Library` value. The only effect-like line in the touched code, `DateOnly.FromDateTime DateTime.Today` in `Payments.pay` (diff line 143), is unchanged context rather than something this change adds. The CLI and persistence do not call into Tier 2.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The allocation rule has one definition, `Accounts.fineCover`. `Payments.pay` and `Views.account` both go through it. `owed` is left as it was, and no literal or predicate is copied.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 55,
                "quote": "| Accounts.Waived(paid, approver) when paid <= 0m -> $\"waived by {approver}\""
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 11,
                "quote": "ensure (not (Accounts.isBlocked (MemberId memberId) library)) (BorrowingBlocked(MemberId memberId))"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The waiver rules are in Tier 2. `Waivers.waive` handles the approver check, target-fine selection and the waived amount. `Accounts.payable` and `fineCover` handle the effect of a waiver on what is owed. A Tier 3 view site then adds its own special case: `Views.account` decides 'nothing paid' with `paid <= 0m` to choose between 'waived by' and 'rest waived by'. This does not contradict Tier 2, but it is a local re-derivation. Separately, the borrow-block check now sits in the Tier 3 `UseCases.borrow` as an `ensure` over the Tier 2 predicate `isBlocked`. That is a clear improvement: the old Tier 4 CLI block with its own 5.00 arithmetic is removed. The guard is still composed in Tier 3 rather than inside `Loans.borrow`.",
            "score": 1
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "`Waivers.waive` is pure and reads no clock. The new borrow guard is pure. The JSON codec change is in the Tier 4 persistence adapter and only serialises the `Waiver` field. The change removes a CLI path that loaded the store directly for the borrow check, since the CLI now calls `UseCases.borrow` only. No new effect goes below Tier 4 and no port is bypassed.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Fines.fs",
                "line": 246,
                "quote": "List.sumBy (fun fine -> fine.Amount - (fine.Waiver |> Option.fold (fun _ w -> w.Amount) 0m))"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "`Accounts.payable` is introduced as the single definition of 'amount net of waiver'. `Fines.outstanding` restates the same expression inline instead of calling it. The two copies currently agree, so this is a restated fact that could drift. The change also removes the old duplicated 5.00 threshold and fines-minus-payments arithmetic from the CLI, which moves the blocking rule onto `Accounts.isBlocked`.",
            "score": 1
          }
        }
      },
